/-
# The cover data of the truncation set `Tset` (tables)

This file fixes the finite tables and the auxiliary definitions used by the proof of
`Work.RTOwed.cuspCert.tset_cover` (in `Submission/Work/RTOwed/cuspCert/tset_cover.lean`).

## What is here

Every point of the truncation set `Tset` is the class of a point on a *truncation facet*
`{truncSlack w = 0} ∩ Qbar` of one of the two copies of `Q̄`.  The facet of the ideal vertex `w` is a
Euclidean cube; each pair `(w, bit)` of a vertex and a copy is one of the 48 cells `a : Fin 48` of
the data `Work.Cusp.Data` (`Work.RTOwed.cubeVert a = w`, `Work.RTOwed.cubeBit a = bit`), and the
facet is the affine image `kleinPt a '' cubeBox a` of its unit cube.

For the cover one reduces a point `q` of the facet to the cube coordinates `x = kleinToX a q ∈
cubeBox a` and then has to replace the (possibly boundary) point `x` by a point `z = x − λ` lying in
the *half-open* cube of a cube `b` of the same cusp: `redV v z = z` then realises `z` as a cusp
coordinate, and the two copies of the facet are glued by the group element `covGam a e`, where `e`
records which of the three coordinates of `x` saturate (`x i = cubeCorner a i + 1`).

The tables:

* `satOf e i` — the saturation pattern of `e : Fin 8`: `1` iff the `i`-th bit of `e` is set;
* `covB a e`, `covK a e` — the neighbour cube `b` and the lattice offsets `k` (so that the shift is
  `λ = diag(latMod v) k`, `latOf`), with `cubeCorner b = cubeCorner a + satOf e − λ`;
* `covS a e`, `covF a e` — the group element `covGam a e ∈ Gg` gluing the cell of `b` at `z` to the
  cell of `a` at `x`: the sign vector and the copy flip;
* `projVZ a` — the direction of the fibre of the projection `π_a = kleinPt a ∘ kleinToX a` (so that
  `projV a = projVZ a / 8` spans `ker π_a`): `π_a y = y + truncSlack (cubeVert a) y • projV a`.

Everything else is the finite verification of these tables (the modules next to this one).

## The certificates (what is left to prove about the tables)

Two tables give *affine identities* that must be verified on the concrete data (finite checks, one
per cube resp. per saturation pattern):

* `projCert (a y)`: `kleinPt a (kleinToX a y) = y + truncSlack (cubeVert a) y • projV a`.  The
  projection `π_a = kleinPt a ∘ kleinToX a` is affine with image the plane of the truncation facet
  of `cubeVert a`, and this identity says that its fibre coordinate is measured by the truncation
  slack.  It is equivalent to the coefficient identities `Π_a = 1 − (1/2) • projV a ⊗ truncNormal2
  (cubeVert a)` and `π_a 0 = (4/5) • projV a` (the `8 • projV a = 10 • π_a 0` of `projVZ`).
* `covAffine (a e x r)`: the expansion, over the saturated coordinates, of the affine function
  `x ↦ covS a e r * kleinPt (covB a e) (zOf a e x) r − kleinPt a x r` (whose coefficients must be
  as recorded in `covC`).

Both are polynomial identities with rational coefficients obtained by unfolding the tables; the
workspace style for such a check is (see `Submission/Work/RTOwed/cuspCertWalls.lean`)

```lean
fin_cases a <;> fin_cases e <;> fin_cases r <;>
  simp only [kleinPt, zOf, covS, covB, covK, covC, latOf, satOf, Work.Cusp.cubeCorner,
    Work.Cusp.cubeXToKlein, Work.Cusp.cubeXToKleinb, Work.Cusp.cubeKleinToX, ...,
    PiLp.toLp_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three, Matrix.cons_val', Matrix.cons_val_zero,
    Matrix.cons_val_one, Matrix.cons_val_fin_one, Matrix.cons_val_two, Matrix.cons_val_three] <;>
  norm_num <;> ring
```

Because `covAffine` has 384 index pairs, it may be necessary to emit one lemma per pair `(a, e)`
(each with four goals `r = 0,1,2,3`) and to combine them with `fin_cases` — the goals are then small
and `ring` closes each of them.

The remaining table facts (`covData`, `cubeLookup`) are integer and group identities that `decide`
can check outright.
-/
